S: 12 CHIP calls in 6 genes (13 other protein changes listed, not counted)
Read-support limit (median 22x over the CHIP genes' coding exons): in the median CHIP gene, a clone with a VAF of about 14% or more shows at least 3 reads with the change 8 times in 10, counted base by base. Mutect2 and its filters call fewer than that. Too few reads for any limit in 2 genes; the share of each one's coding bases read deep enough for that VAF: JAK2 0%, TET2 0%. CHIP starts at a VAF of 2%, so smaller clones are likely missed: no call here does not rule one out. Not a diagnosis.
